        <body>
            <div xml:id="d279">

                <pb facs="0563" n="507" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg507"/>

                <head>No. 269.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Cushing to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-12-01"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 1, 1874</date>.
                        (Received December 26.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 171.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith copy of a note addressed
                    by me to Mr. Ulloa yesterday, insisting on the arraignment, in conformity with
                    stipulation by protocol, of local authorities implicated in the transactions at
                    Santiago de Cuba. I trust nothing will have been lost by the omission to make
                    this point in previous notes. Indeed, it seems to me quite opportune at the
                    present time.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>C. CUSHING.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d279-a1.xml" xpointer="d279-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
